    description: "A classic from the Dauphiné region of south-east France. Thinly sliced waxy potatoes layered in a garlic-rubbed dish, seasoned with salt, pepper, and nutmeg, drowned in cream, and baked slowly until the potatoes are tender and the top is bubbling and bronzed. No cheese in the orthodox version — cheese turns it into gratin savoyard.",
